Hmm — `.gitignore.public` is used by publish-docs.bat as template for public repo; keep it ignored in private? The bat reads it from working dir (`%~dp0.gitignore.public`) — ignoring it in git is fine since it reads from disk not git. But does the file exist? Check. Also `allatori.jar` — keep tracked (needed for builds, private repo OK).

Wait, should I exclude allatori.jar? It's a commercial tool (demo). Committing to private repo is user's choice — they said private repo to protect code; allatori.jar in private repo is fine and needed for reproducible builds. Keep it.

